# Transport and browser boundary

## Listeners

- New public listeners use TLS. Do not add a plaintext admin port on a public
  interface
- Bind admin and debug endpoints to the narrowest interface that still works
- Leave certificate verification on for outbound clients

## Browsers

- Session cookies: `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, and the strictest `SameSite` the
  product allows
- Cross-origin configuration lists explicit origins. Do not combine a
  wildcard origin with credentialed requests
- State-changing cookie requests need a cross-site request check
- Set `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. Set a frame policy and a referrer
  policy when adding a new public site
- Add a content security policy only when the project already has one, or when
  the page is new and the policy is tested. A copied policy that blocks the
  app is not a control
- Do not reflect untrusted input into headers
